    "legend": "The bone marrow biopsy (&lt;&lt;36810&gt;&gt;) is hypercellular for age and shows an erythroid predominance and atypical megakaryocytic hyperplasia, with increased large and hyperlobulated megakaryocytes forming loose clusters. The bone marrow aspirate smears (&lt;&lt;36806&gt;&gt;, &lt;&lt;36807&gt;&gt;) show increased large, hyperlobulated megakaryocytes (&lt;&lt;36807&gt;&gt;) and increased erythroid precursors, many with features of maturation asynchrony, and occasional hypogranular neutrophils (shown here). Next-generation sequencing of this sample showed the following mutations: <em>SF3B1</em> p.K700E, <em>JAK2</em> p.V617F, and <em>ASXL1</em> p.G646fs and p.R693*.",
