    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Diagnostic criteria for myelodysplastic/myeloproliferative neoplasm (MDS/MPN) with ring sideroblasts and thrombocytosis</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Eric Solary",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"background: #daeef3; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Peripheral blood:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Anaemia (haemoglobin below the normal range)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Thrombocytosis (platelet count &gt;&nbsp;450&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;10<sup>9</sup>/L)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No or very rare blast cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Bone marrow cytology:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Dysplasia, especially dyserythropoiesis with ring sideroblasts </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{10492088; 6619310; 25899435; 16741247}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Molecular analyses of blood or bone marrow:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">SF3B1</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> heterozygous mutation</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Concurrent <em>JAK2</em> p.V617F or, in the absence of <em>JAK2</em> p.V617F, mutation in another myeloproliferative gene such as <em>MPL</em> or <em>CALR</em> </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{16926301; 16932338; 17244688; 19692701; 25957392; 22096241; 16670082; 16990759; 11940483; 17713548; 17194663; 16741247; 16871284}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">If molecular analyses are unavailable:</span></em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 33.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"45\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 673.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"898\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Peripheral blood:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 30.05pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Sustained thrombocytosis for &ge;&nbsp;3&nbsp;months substitutes <em>JAK2</em>, <em>MPL</em>, or <em>CALR</em> mutation</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 33.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"45\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 673.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"898\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Bone marrow cytology:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 30.05pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&ge;&nbsp;15% ring sideroblasts substitutes <em>SF3B1</em> mutation</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 60.3pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 60.3pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">To be excluded:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Therapy-related myeloid neoplasms</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">MDS with isolated del(5q)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Myeloid neoplasms with a double-hit <em>TP53</em> alteration</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Myeloid neoplasms with t(3;3)(q21.3;q26.2) or inv(3)(q21.3q26.2)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Disease-defining gene fusions such as <em>BCR</em>::<em>ABL1</em></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 56.8pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 56.8pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Specific situation:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 1cm; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Rare cases that initially present as a myeloid neoplasm with <em>SF3B1</em> mutation and ring sideroblasts and later evolve to MDS/MPN with ring sideroblasts and thrombocytosis upon acquisition of a <em>JAK2</em>, <em>MPL</em>, or <em>CALR</em> mutation may be classified as MDS/MPN with <em>SF3B1</em> mutation and thrombocytosis </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{19692701}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\">MDS, myelodysplastic neoplasm.</span></p>",
